# comments
0100 reset vector: SEI, reset stack, set up ports
011b PA5 = on/off switch sense; $20 = power state (0x11 off, 0x99 on)
013e compare RAM copy of option bytes with EPROM 1F2E/1F33..1F37 (warm start?)
016c copy EPROM 1F2E..1F31 -> RAM $2B..$2E ($2E = current channel = lowest channel)
0181 copy option bytes 1F33..1F37 -> RAM $2F..$33
0190 STOP: wait for wake-up (IRQ)
01dc builds "ADD $hhll,X; RTS" in RAM $21 and sums $0100-$1FFF; must equal $FF
0238 timer: TDR=$FF, TCR=$0F
025d 1FA9 -> $C8 (selcall timing)
0274 tell control head we (re)started
02fe PA6 = PTT input (inferred)
030f PA7 = second front input (hook/monitor, inferred)
036f timer reload: TDR=$C5, TCR=$09 -> ~2.4 kHz tick (one tick ~415 us)
0377 PB5 high (synth strobe idle; strobes are low-going pulses)
037e PB1 toggles every tick (1.2 kHz square wave)
038a 16-entry slot table, one slot every 2 ticks
0842 X=2: Rx bytes 0-2, X=5: Tx bytes 3-5 of the channel slot
0858 bit7 of byte2/5 = entry valid, else carry set = empty channel
086d Rx: byte2 bit4 (C/R) -> $1B.5 / $19.2
0875 Rx: byte2 bit5 (VOTE) handled in chan_flags_rx
0878 Rx: byte2 bit3 -> latch $2C bit5 (VCO band switch)
0882 bit6 (injection side) -> $29.1
0890 synth: port A = 1F2D, PB6 high (enable), 2 strobes
089b synth: 4 BCD digits, low nibble then high nibble, one PB5 strobe each
08aa synth: digit 5 (byte2/5 | 8)
08b0 synth: then reference bytes 1F2C, 1F2D; PB6 low again
08c7 ptr = $1BE0 + 8*A  (into RAM routine at $21: LDA $hhll,X; RTS)
0800 bytes 6,7 of slot -> $34 (CTCSS/flags), $35 (link)
080e byte5 bit3 -> latch $82 bit5
0822 byte5 bits4-5 = power; 0 -> operator-selected power from $2C
08f8 software UART on PB0: ~1200 baud 8E1 (start, 8 data LSB first, even parity, stop), single wire idle-high; PB0 is driven only while sending; 4-byte TX FIFO $3D-$40
09e2 ADC: select mux via $2A latch, note start time; IRQ (comparator) stores result
09fb squelch: pot ($49) -> setting 0-7 via table $0A4C (with hysteresis)
0a74 noise ($45) vs close threshold 1F1C+setting
0a8e noise ($45) vs open threshold 1F14+setting
0a85 squelch tail from table 1F24
0ae9 soft timers: $57-$61,$E9,$EA every 64 ticks (~27 ms)
0b0d $63-$65,$EB,$EC every 2304 ticks (~1 s)
0b20 $67 every 24064 ticks (~10 s): Tx timer / auto power-off units
0b32 latch $2C (inverted) -> port A, PB4 strobe: power level, VCO band etc.
0b80 signature over firmware + 1F65, and 1F33..1F37 + 1F66: must be 0 else halt
0bae on failure jump to $0189 (power down / stop)
0bb1 IRQ = ADC comparator: result = start_time - timer - $1E
0be5 queue byte for control head (wait while FIFO full)
0c24 send 2 display digits: $80/$81 + char, $82/$83 + char
0c95 Tx: forward-power ADC ($4A) must lie in window 1F08..1F0F for current power level
0cac Rx: $4A < $15 -> supply too low: shut down with alarm on PA4
0ccb window check: 1F00+x <= A <= 1F01+x
0d36 CTCSS code (byte6 bits0-5) -> tone chip value table $0E56 -> $81
0d45 copy selcall codes 1F67..1F70 -> $CA.., 1F7A..1F83 -> $D4..
0e7d scanning: lists via $53/$54 pointer (1F40 block 1, 1F4C block 2)
0f62 compare noise $45 with open threshold 1F14+squelch setting
1067 RAM routine LDA list,X  (X=0 priority channel, X=11 count)
1077 scan list base table: 1F40, 1F4C
108e voting: hop round the linked ring (byte7 & $7F)+1, compare RSSI ($46)
10fb 1FB4 = vote/scan dwell time
1129 1F1B = voting threshold
1142 selcall decoder: reads tone digit from $80, compares with 1F8D/1F96/1F9F codes
11de selcall encoder: sends digits with timing from 1F70/1F71
14d1 economiser: power-save cycling with times 1FB1/1FB2/1FB3
1557 8-hour auto power off: 1FB5 x 30 min (enabled by 1F35 bit5)
157e command $4A from head: dump RAM to head (diagnostic)
158c init external peripherals $80-$86
